**Read:** [Introduction to Mining Engineering — Penn State MNG 230](../sources/Penn-State-Introduction-to-Mining.lingua#r_5NAY6K47Y4Y61V4JF74JJNV4Q2), the complete terminology/evaluation introduction; [Tratamento de Minérios — CETEM, sixth edition](../sources/Tratamento-de-Minerios-CETEM.lingua#r_04ZQFADZ3NC3T6QDPQ565W1ERA), the complete introductory processing and balance/characterization material; [Resources, reserves, and technical-study definitions — CRIRSCO and CBRR](../sources/Resource-and-Reserve-Reporting-CRIRSCO-CBRR.lingua#r_2CZZ64T1W8VC542VCNCH2E6DSR), the full definitions and scope sections.

Define deposit, mineralization, ore, waste, overburden, dilution, loss, run-of-mine feed, concentrate, middlings, tailings, recovery, and product specification in the actual context. Similar words can refer to geological, engineering, processing, commercial, or reporting categories with different evidence requirements.

Grade may be elemental mass fraction, oxide-equivalent content, a valuable-mineral proportion, energy content, or a physical-quality measure. Recovery needs an identified constituent, feed/product boundaries, period, and mass basis. Mass yield, metal recovery, concentration ratio, and product purity answer different questions.

Material can be described on wet, dry, as-received, size-fraction, or other bases. Percent moisture can itself use different denominators. A stream with a stated grade and tonnage is incomplete unless the basis, sampling, measurement, and time aggregation are known.

**Work:** build an original glossary from a complete processing chapter and mine case, giving a quantity/basis and an example for each consequential term. Translate selected Portuguese/English terms and explain where a literal translation hides a different convention. Reconstruct a reported recovery and show which inputs would be needed to check it.

Read full definitions and examples rather than memorizing abbreviations. The later balance and accounting studies make these distinctions quantitative, while reporting categories remain tied to their identified primary definitions.

